ition was still  a good strategy for the company the  court also said that shareholders would  be better served on the whole by a  specific performance remedy rather than  a large damages award that did nothing  but cost tyson a large amount of money  and now i need to explain some trivia  about the delaware courts of chancery  where this case is going to end up  if you've been paying attention to  litigation you often hear people say  it'll take years to resolve anything and  that's usually the case that is not the  case in the delaware chancery courts the  delaware chance reports are basically  business courts on steroids they handle  mergers and acquisitions for breakfast  and delaware made a name for itself by  being the most business-friendly state  in the country and the delaware chance  records have a specific expertise  in dealing with these enormous business  disputes and they are fast this could  end up being resolved in months rather  than years and while the numbers are  very high the dollar amounts are very  high this is not a particularly complex  case uh in fact  elon musk is incredibly online so so  many of the statements that he has made  are  public and will absolutely be used  against him so we'll probably have an  answer to this question pretty quickly  and at base the litigation outcomes are  pretty stark  one billion dollars in damages or force  musk to pay 44 billion dollars to  acquire a company he doesn't want now in  reality depending on how litigation goes  i'm sure all of the parties will  probably negotiate something in between  maybe a bigger fee that lets elon walk  away uh or maybe a lower price and he  consummates the deal it's entirely  possible that everything was just  posturing for him to get a better deal  in the long term or maybe elon never  wanted twitter in the first place who  knows but the important thing is that  lawyers are going to get paid  and speaking of which there is the  breaking news that twitter has indeed  sued